{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Upon the head of the burnt offering.</b> To bring an obligatory burnt offering for semikhah and to bring a burnt offering of the flock (there)." "<b>The burnt offering.</b> This specifies the burnt offering of a bird (there)." "<b>And it shall be accepted for him.</b> For what does it effect acceptance for him? If you say for karetot and court-imposed deaths or death by the hand of Heaven or lashes — behold their punishment is stated; rather, it effects acceptance only for a positive commandment and for a negative commandment turned into a positive commandment (there)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:35.316130701Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}